Review written to `docs/reviews/envelope-rc-mat/rc-mat-02-rc-network-discretization.md`.

**Key findings:**

- **Finding 1 [HIGH]**: Same-zone boundary orientation is reversed in the material-layer path (`build_layered_boundary`). The cut (symmetry-plane) side connects to zone air with an incorrect exterior-film resistance, while the actual interior-facing side is dead-ended. The precomputed (OCHRE LUT) path correctly connects the interior side. The fix is guarding `boundary_rc.rs:1273` with `!params.same_zone` and removing the guard on the interior wiring at `boundary_rc.rs:1298`.

- **Finding 2 [MEDIUM]**: `split_layer_count` has no upper bound. Thick walls (>1.5 m) could produce >20 nodes per construction, exceeding practical limits.

- **Finding 3 [LOW]**: Minimum RC time constant is ~1 ms (R ≥ 1e-6 K/W, C ≥ 1000 J/K). ZOH exact discretization absorbs this stiffness, but the frozen-fast-mode behavior merits documentation.

- **Findings 4-5**: Observability confirmed (no orphaned thermal mass); determinism confirmed (timestep-independent diurnal criterion).
